Review these previously model-flagged conflict pairs against the supplied quotations and scope/date fields. Do not assume every pair is a conflict. Different products, origins, tariff programs, or dated stages are not automatically contradictory. Only use apparent_same_scope_conflict when the supplied claims appear incompatible on the same scope/date; otherwise distinguish dated progression, differing scope, complementary claims, and missing scope. Do not verify current law from memory. Explain the reason briefly for every pair.
UNTRUSTED_EVIDENCE_JSON:
{"research_date": "2026-09-10", "pairs": [{"pair_id": "conflict_1bc1d78091311dd85dcf8796", "claim_ids": ["claim_3ff049100bbe98cd71a14d73", "claim_79899bfb5bc501811d486e18"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_3ff049100bbe98cd71a14d73", "quote": "Therefore, US customs authorities later reclassified these vehicles as transport vehicles based on their features and intended use. This reclassification led to allegations of false declarations by Ford, potentially resulting in over $1 billion in additional tariffs.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "legal_authority": "US customs authorities", "affected_product": "vehicles"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_79899bfb5bc501811d486e18", "quote": "Merritt v. Welsh, held that tariff engineering is an acceptable practice.", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "Merritt v. Welsh", "reported_policy_status": "acceptable practice"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_93751ecc3dfc7952efe76bd6", "claim_ids": ["claim_4b607639a630dfe9aab30b51", "claim_a6cdf42442a3d5377b56cda0"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_4b607639a630dfe9aab30b51", "quote": "Between 2009 and 2013, Ford imported over 160,000 Transit Connect vehicles. Before importation, Ford installed second-row seats in order to classify them as passenger cars, which carried a 2.5% tariff rate, avoiding the high tariff rate of 25% for transport vehicles.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "duty_rate": "2.5%"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_a6cdf42442a3d5377b56cda0", "quote": "As part of the settlement, Ford agreed to pay $365 million to resolve the DOJ action.", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "duty_rate": "$365 million"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_3ceac8799c018cc9865e0219", "claim_ids": ["claim_bcf32fcb59aa6b44dac6041d", "claim_cf7c8ffe65a67501fbae49de"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_bcf32fcb59aa6b44dac6041d", "quote": "Last year, Ford settled the dispute by agreeing to pay $365 million and committed to obtaining binding customs rulings for future models, while also withdrawing its lawsuit challenging the classification.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "duty_rate": "$365 million"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_cf7c8ffe65a67501fbae49de", "quote": "As background, Ford manufactured the Transit Connect vehicles in Turkey and imported them into the United States.", "url": "https://scalirasmussen.com/insight/2025/02/25/tariff-engineering", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"company": "Ford", "facility": "Turkey"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_89d44a54b99294cf6b7e158f", "claim_ids": ["claim_3b0c5aa321b3b624b856b937", "claim_9640e77589a6b57234a13e5f"], "query_ids": ["q_473"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_3b0c5aa321b3b624b856b937", "quote": "Also in Switzerland, this distinction led to several fines and reclassifications of pick-up trucks over the past years, as besides customs duties, particularly the automobile tax plays a vital role.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_9640e77589a6b57234a13e5f", "quote": "According to the HS Committee of the World Customs Organization, pick-ups are not considered vehicles for the transport of goods due to their relatively small loading areas.", "url": "https://www.pwc.ch/en/insights/custom-ised/tariff-engineering-customs-optimisation.html", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"legal_authority": "HS Committee of the World Customs Organization"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_266a2a776ce073b760c6d67d", "claim_ids": ["claim_6855560ba5b2d7d5d210b23d", "claim_9ff0feb7f32297e1d91e037d"], "query_ids": ["q_474"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_6855560ba5b2d7d5d210b23d", "quote": "President Trump's implementation of a 40% penalty tariff on transshipped goods, effective August 7, 2025.", "url": "https://www.e2open.com/blog/navigating-the-transshipment-crisis", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "40% penalty tariff on transshipped goods", "duty_rate": "40%", "effective_date": "August 7, 2025", "reported_policy_status": "implementation"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_9ff0feb7f32297e1d91e037d", "quote": "the Trump administration has indicated that, under some of the preliminary trade agreements it has reached with several countries, U.S. imports of goods transshipped through those countries may be subject to an additional 40 percent tariff.", "url": "https://www.strtrade.com/trade-news-resources/str-trade-report/trade-report/september/cbp-identifies-red-flags-best-practices-on-transshipping", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {"tariff_program": "preliminary trade agreements", "duty_rate": "40 percent", "reported_policy_status": "indicated"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_41d1eb6ffdefae635296fc4e", "claim_ids": ["claim_08ff06926ad3fb5a2c67d8ac", "claim_e7bc12cb626624b0ec81e403"], "query_ids": ["q_475"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_08ff06926ad3fb5a2c67d8ac", "quote": "Price adjustment clauses are your safety valve when supplier costs spike. Without them, vendors may have no obligation to absorb tariff-related increases, or worse, they might pass them straight on to you with no warning.", "url": "https://www.docusign.com/blog/tariffs-impact-8-important-clauses-to-check-for-in-your-supplier-agreements", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_e7bc12cb626624b0ec81e403", "quote": "Nearly all suppliers say they plan pass through 100% of the tariff impact to the manufacturers.", "url": "https://www.eatonvance.com/insights/articles/how-do-automotive-tariffs-impact-the-auto-corporate-sector.html", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_80c063aa6944a709c0ef2fd2", "claim_ids": ["claim_6c42dea0c8cf670975e22bb9", "claim_d7fe3e06a5f7841ec1ec9efa"], "query_ids": ["q_475"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_6c42dea0c8cf670975e22bb9", "quote": "Tier 1 suppliers are likely to achieve something close to this, but Tier 2 and Tier 3 suppliers will struggle and will need to share some of the pain.", "url": "https://www.eatonvance.com/insights/articles/how-do-automotive-tariffs-impact-the-auto-corporate-sector.html", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}, {"claim_id": "claim_d7fe3e06a5f7841ec1ec9efa", "quote": "The original equipment manufacturers (OEM)s will likely be forced to support critical suppliers that may struggle with the tariff impact, as they did during the post-COVID-19 shutdown supply chain shocks.", "url": "https://www.eatonvance.com/insights/articles/how-do-automotive-tariffs-impact-the-auto-corporate-sector.html", "kind": "search_snippet", "publisher_type": "secondary_or_unverified_publisher", "fields": {}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_9e594e4eb601323485aeba0a", "claim_ids": ["claim_09aafdefb421cf062a3c402b", "claim_44aedcbe21306bdbe3c42eb7"], "query_ids": ["q_476"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_09aafdefb421cf062a3c402b", "quote": "imposing tariffs of 100 percent on certain ship-to-shore cranes and cargo handling equipment.", "url": "https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2025/october/ustr-modifies-certain-aspects-section-301-ships-action-and-proposes-further-modifications-action", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"affected_product": "ship-to-shore cranes and cargo handling equipment", "duty_rate": "100 percent", "effective_date": "October 14, 2025"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_44aedcbe21306bdbe3c42eb7", "quote": "the U.S. Trade Representative has determined to impose additional duties of 100 percent on STS cranes as described in Annex V.A to this notice", "url": "https://ustr.gov/sites/default/files/files/Press/Releases/2025/301%20Ships%20Action%20Mod%20FRN.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"duty_rate": "100 percent", "effective_date": "April 17, 2025"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_b6e969e36512cc29b2b8e906", "claim_ids": ["claim_05a82eb4e975a0df5e77df29", "claim_0f00d987a85c219547b30dd4"], "query_ids": ["q_476"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_05a82eb4e975a0df5e77df29", "quote": "impose additional tariffs of up to 150 percent on other cargo handling equipment, including: rubber tire gantry cranes, rail mounted gantry cranes, automatic staking cranes, reachstackers, straddle carriers, terminal tractors, top handlers (which may also be referred to as top loaders), and parts of these machines.", "url": "https://ustr.gov/sites/default/files/files/Press/Releases/2025/301%20Ships%20Action%20Mod%20FRN.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"duty_rate": "up to 150 percent", "announcement_date": "April 18, 2029"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_0f00d987a85c219547b30dd4", "quote": "Annex V.B: Add a new Annex V.B and impose additional tariffs of up to 150 percent on other cargo handling equipment, including: rubber tire gantry cranes, rail mounted gantry cranes, automatic staking cranes, reachstackers, straddle carriers, terminal tractors, top handlers (which may also be referred to as top loaders), and parts of these machines.", "url": "https://ustr.gov/sites/default/files/files/Press/Releases/2025/301%20Ships%20Action%20Mod%20FRN.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"affected_product": "rubber tire gantry cranes, rail mounted gantry cranes, automatic staking cranes, reachstackers, straddle carriers, terminal tractors, top handlers (which may also be referred to as top loaders), and parts of these machines", "duty_rate": "up to 150 percent"}}]}, {"pair_id": "conflict_90bf35e928044ee2c0172674", "claim_ids": ["claim_7969f3829a7336ee3009ca33", "claim_7db67bc00acfe03b44d35c67"], "query_ids": ["q_476"], "claims": [{"claim_id": "claim_7969f3829a7336ee3009ca33", "quote": "imposing additional tariffs of up to 150 percent on certain cargo handling equipment (e.g., rubber tire gantry cranes) and components of such equipment.", "url": "https://ustr.gov/about/policy-offices/press-office/press-releases/2025/october/ustr-modifies-certain-aspects-section-301-ships-action-and-proposes-further-modifications-action", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"affected_product": "cargo handling equipment (e.g., rubber tire gantry cranes) and components of such equipment", "duty_rate": "up to 150 percent"}}, {"claim_id": "claim_7db67bc00acfe03b44d35c67", "quote": "imposing additional duties of 100 percent on ship-to-shore (STS) cranes and duties of 100 percent on certain cargo handling equipment of China as described in Annex V.A of this notice.", "url": "https://ustr.gov/sites/default/files/files/Press/Releases/2025/301%20Ships%20Action%20Mod%20FRN.pdf", "kind": "full_document", "publisher_type": "official_trade_authority", "fields": {"tariff_program": "Section 301 Action", "affected_product": "certain cargo handling equipment", "duty_rate": "100 percent"}}]}]}

